/*--------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  MEASURED vapour-liquid equilibrium of ethylene (1) + ethane (2) at 293.15 K.

  SOURCE (the page, not an archive): Fredenslund, A.; Mollerup, J.; Hall, K.R.
  "Vapor-liquid equilibria of the CO2-ethylene-ethane system", J. Chem. Eng.
  Data 21 (1976) 301-303 (the PDF opens on the tail of the previous article),
  Table I "Vapor-Liquid Equilibrium in the C2H4 + C2H6 System" (p. 302), the
  EXPERIMENTAL columns P, x and y, read from the page image at 220 dpi.  The
  paper's footnote: mole fractions are given with four significant figures
  to avoid round-off, and are "only believed accurate to within 0.003".  The
  vapour was SAMPLED (vapour-recirculation cell).  Pressure in atm.
  293.15 K is ABOVE the critical temperature of ethylene (282.34 K, the catalogue record): there is no
  pure liquid ethylene, the paper uses the unsymmetric convention (Henry's
  constant 38.0 atm) for its own calculation, and the measurements stop at
  x = 0.4532.  The engine's cubic needs no convention: the mixture is one
  fluid, its bubble pressure is the pressure at which the liquid composition
  of the row meets a vapour of its own.

  Columns are the props bench's overlay names: x[ethylene], P_bubble,
  y_eqT_ethylene; `alpha` is alpha = (y1/x1)/(y2/x2) of the measured pair,
  kept for the gate (bin/curate/check_olefin_vle.py).  Pure ends are not listed
  (y = x there).  The CALCULATED columns of the paper's Table I are not used.
\*--------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

property     binaryVLE.P_bubble;
system       ( ethylene ethane );
temperature  293.15 K;

provenance
{
    source       measured;
    reviewStatus transcribedNotCheckedAgainstArticle;
    citation     "Fredenslund, A.; Mollerup, J.; Hall, K.R. (1976). Vapor-liquid equilibria of the carbon dioxide-ethylene-ethane system. J. Chem. Eng. Data 21, 301-303, Table I (p. 302). doi:10.1021/je60070a006";
    sourceFile   "fredenslund1976-co2-ethylene-ethane-vle.pdf";
    sha256       "a85b71ce08f2f5ede6d3c3e41daabdef3acf1a1f12de8bdf3bdf5f24c6c4ba07";   // of that PDF
}

uncertainty
{
    x_and_y
    {
        kind    statedBound;   // the paper's footnote, a bound not a confidence level
        unit    -;
        value   0.003;
    }
}

columns
(
    { name x[ethylene];  unit -;  }
    { name P_bubble;  unit atm;  }
    { name y_eqT_ethylene;  unit -;  }
    { name alpha;  unit -;  }
);

data
(
    0.0539  38.46  0.0662  1.2444
    0.1537  40.85  0.1772  1.1858
    0.2663  43.57  0.2968  1.1629
    0.3664  45.98  0.3936  1.1224
    0.3988  46.85  0.4251  1.1147
    0.4532  47.85  0.4722  1.0794
);
